# Working style

Read `AGENTS.md` first: it holds the project rules, checks and commit format. This file adds
how the owner likes to work. `docs/status.md` lists open work outside the online plan.

## Understand the request

- The owner writes short messages, often with a screenshot. Read the screenshot carefully: it
  usually shows the screen or the previous agent's last message the request refers to.
- "Next" or "continue" means the next unticked step in the relevant plan: `docs/online.md`
  (online play), the README's multiplayer roadmap, or `docs/status.md`. Check `git log -10`
  to see what was done last before starting.
- If a request is ambiguous and the answer changes what you build, ask one short question.
  Otherwise pick the sensible default, say which you picked, and go.
- Decisions in `docs/decisions.md` are agreed with the owner. Don't reverse one without
  asking; record new decisions there.

## Keep usage low

- One task per session. When it is done, say so in one line and suggest starting a new chat.
- Before a long investigation (more than a few steps), give a short plan and ask if it is
  worth it.
- Read only the needed part of big files; keep command output short (`tail`, `grep`, `head`).
- While working run only targeted tests; the full suite once before a push.
- A flaky test: at most two tries to reproduce, then report and ask.

## Doing the work

- UI work: read `docs/design.md`, reuse existing components, build the same thing on Android
  and iOS. For a new screen or a big redesign, agree on a mockup with the owner before code.
- Every user-facing string in English and Indonesian (see `AGENTS.md`). No hardcoded strings.
- Game rules only in `shared/`; congklak must match the traditional game (clockwise sowing,
  each player's store on their left).
- No simulator or emulator: the Mac is small. Build for the connected iPhone 17 or Pixel XL
  with `./scripts/install-ios.sh` / `./scripts/install-android.sh` (see `docs/install.md`).
  If none is connected, just build and ask the owner to check on the device.
- iOS builds need JDK 21 for the shared framework: `JAVA_HOME=$(/usr/libexec/java_home -v 21)`
  (or Homebrew `openjdk@21`). Gradle needs JDK 17–21, not Android Studio's JDK 25.
- Run the checks from `AGENTS.md` for every part you touched. Report results honestly: if a
  check failed or you couldn't run it, say so. Never claim a device test you didn't do.

## Finishing

- Tick or update the step in `docs/online.md` / README roadmap / `docs/status.md` in the same
  commit as the work, so the next session can pick up from the repo alone.
- Commit only when the owner asks (or the task clearly includes it). Conventional Commits, see
  `AGENTS.md`.
- Never add `Co-Authored-By`, "Generated with …" or any AI attribution to commits or PRs.
- Pushing to `main` deploys whatever the workflows in `.github/workflows/` cover (the relay,
  the web site). Mention that before pushing relay or web changes.
- Reply short: what changed, what was checked, what is still open, the next step.

## Releases

- TestFlight / App Store: build and upload yourself with
  `xcrun altool --upload-app --type ios -f <ipa> --apiKey "$ASC_KEY_ID" --apiIssuer "$ASC_ISSUER_ID"`
  (key in `~/.appstoreconnect/private_keys/`, env vars in `~/.zshenv`). Use a build number
  higher than the last upload.
- Don't upload to Play internal testing until several games are ready.
